  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "QP1pTSZ8go82OYtNCdxGZiC8HdI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:10.289Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The sequence recorded is: identify the companion software; build a demo with Powerhouse integration; produce social media and marketing materials from it (a YouTube recording of the demo, blog and LinkedIn posts, tweet threads, mini-sites and landing pages for SEO and agent traffic); run a conversion funnel to introduction calls; and actively target consultancy companies using that software.\n\nThe design point is that the demo is the raw material for everything downstream \u2014 the recording, the posts, the landing pages and the sales conversation are all derivatives of one artefact. That makes demo quality the leverage point of the whole motion.\n\nBecause the sequence is keyed to a piece of software rather than to an industry, it can be re-run per companion tool, which is what makes it a repeatable machine rather than a campaign.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T10:34:10.289918Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:10.289923Z"
    }
  },
